# The A28 definition manifest is compared against its generator's output
# BYTE-for-byte (src/MechaMiner.Tools/ContentImport/verify_content.py, A28), and
# the generator writes LF via write_bytes(). Pinning eol=lf here keeps a checkout
# from converting the file to CRLF on a platform that otherwise would, which
# would redden the gate without anything being wrong with the content.
#
# Scoped to this one path on purpose: it is the only file in the tree whose exact
# bytes an assertion depends on.
src/MechaMiner.Tools/ContentImport/content-definition-manifest.txt text eol=lf
